      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision). A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. That's true even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO twice daily.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, the typical analgesic or antipyretic dosing.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale for the order note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
